1
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:07,170
Nintendo Switch Sports shows a win
banner and a celebration after a match.

2
00:00:07,480 --> 00:00:11,850
Ring Fit Adventure accompanies exercise
movements with evaluation feedback.

3
00:00:12,180 --> 00:00:16,310
The same score can feel different
when a game acknowledges what you did.

4
00:00:16,620 --> 00:00:20,710
We can distinguish calculating success from
expressing recognition of that success.

5
00:00:21,100 --> 00:00:26,050
Today we examine how to recognize an
action, rather than how to add rewards.

6
00:00:26,660 --> 00:00:30,745
Our original defense test applies the same
inputs and collision rules to both screens.

7
00:00:30,760 --> 00:00:34,330
We change the timing, wording, strength, and position of the praise.

8
00:00:34,700 --> 00:00:39,150
Enjoyment needs human testing, while
logs can verify exactly what changed.

9
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:42,330
First, compare when the praise appears.

10
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:45,870
Both characters block the same attack at the same moment.

11
00:00:46,040 --> 00:00:49,730
One side responds promptly; the other responds much later.

12
00:00:49,860 --> 00:00:54,410
If the next attack arrives during the wait, it
is harder to connect praise with the action.

13
00:00:54,580 --> 00:00:58,190
Try attaching a brief response close
to the successful collision result.

14
00:00:58,320 --> 00:01:02,690
The signal can acknowledge the recent
action without a large display.

15
00:01:02,900 --> 00:01:05,905
This does not prescribe one delay for every game.

16
00:01:05,920 --> 00:01:10,730
It is a reason to check overlap with
the next action at normal speed.

17
00:01:11,520 --> 00:01:15,570
A generic compliment may not explain what went well.

18
00:01:15,780 --> 00:01:19,790
This test blocks an attack, then moves upward to dodge the next one.

19
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:24,910
One screen repeats the same praise; the
other distinguishes blocking from dodging.

20
00:01:25,060 --> 00:01:28,330
A brief label names the action actually
verified by the collision rules.

21
00:01:28,600 --> 00:01:33,350
Calling a button press a perfect block can misrepresent the result.

22
00:01:33,600 --> 00:01:37,290
Choose the label from the successful
outcome, rather than the input event alone.

23
00:01:37,660 --> 00:01:41,330
That information can help the player
identify an action to try again.

24
00:01:41,520 --> 00:01:46,030
Praise need not become an instruction
manual, but it need not hide its reason.

25
00:01:46,720 --> 00:01:50,970
Using the largest celebration for every
success removes a distinction between moments.

26
00:01:51,160 --> 00:01:56,250
A match win in Switch Sports illustrates
a broader celebration at a stopping point.

27
00:01:56,520 --> 00:02:01,170
The same scale after every small
success can cover the next situation.

28
00:02:01,280 --> 00:02:04,550
Our test uses a small marker for a single block.

29
00:02:04,680 --> 00:02:08,425
A stronger response appears only when a
sequence of successful blocks is verified.

30
00:02:08,440 --> 00:02:12,630
The score and successful-action count stay
equal; only presentation strength changes.

31
00:02:12,900 --> 00:02:16,630
Distinguish an individual success, a sequence,
and the completion of a longer section.

32
00:02:16,720 --> 00:02:20,970
This aligns the scale of the recognition
with the actual accomplishment.

33
00:02:21,760 --> 00:02:26,090
Unconditionally calling a failure perfect
can undermine trust in the praise.

34
00:02:26,300 --> 00:02:30,430
Both screens receive the same inputs,
deliberately missing one attack.

35
00:02:30,680 --> 00:02:34,830
Health falls equally, but one side still
claims the performance was perfect.

36
00:02:35,020 --> 00:02:39,110
The other side shows the hit and acknowledges
only the blocks that actually succeeded.

37
00:02:39,340 --> 00:02:43,590
We can name a genuine partial success without hiding the failure.

38
00:02:43,820 --> 00:02:46,250
Every failure does not need a compliment.

39
00:02:46,520 --> 00:02:50,725
Show a retry clue separately, and
distinguish signals for success and failure.

40
00:02:50,740 --> 00:02:55,230
Supportive wording should remain connected
to actual outcomes to inform another attempt.

41
00:02:56,160 --> 00:03:00,110
Finally, check whether the praise obstructs the next action.

42
00:03:00,420 --> 00:03:05,170
Large text placed over the attack can cover
the area where the next threat must be read.

43
00:03:05,360 --> 00:03:09,830
This comparison preserves outcomes and
wording while changing position and area.

44
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:13,830
Compare a small marker near the action
with a brief response near the edge.

45
00:03:14,240 --> 00:03:18,710
Check that neither moving targets nor necessary
information are obscured at phone size.

46
00:03:18,860 --> 00:03:23,625
Record what is recognized, when it is
recognized, and how strongly it is expressed.

47
00:03:23,640 --> 00:03:28,550
Before increasing praise frequency, check
whether the expression matches the recent action.

48
00:03:28,880 --> 00:03:33,350
Look for moments of accomplishment in
the actual actions of your own game.
